{title: It Came Upon the Midnight Clear}
{artist: Edmund H. Sears / Richard S. Willis}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Carol}
{key: G}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 6/8}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 112장}
{title_ko: 그 맑고 환한 밤중에}
{score: it-came-upon-the-midnight-clear.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
It [G]came upon the [D]midnight [G]clear
That [C]glorious song of [G]old
From [G]angels bending [D]near the [G]earth
To [C]touch their harps of [D]gold
"[G]Peace on the [C]earth, good [G]will to men
From [Am]heaven's all-gra[D]cious King"
The [G]world in solemn [D]stillness [G]lay
To [C]hear the [D]angels [G]sing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Still [G]through the cloven [D]skies they [G]come
With [C]peaceful wings un[G]furled
And [G]still their heavenly [D]music [G]floats
O'er [C]all the weary [D]world
A[G]bove its sad and [C]lowly [G]plains
They [Am]bend on hovering [D]wing
And [G]ever o'er its [D]Babel [G]sounds
The [C]blessed [D]angels [G]sing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
And [G]ye, beneath life's [D]crushing [G]load
Whose [C]forms are bending [G]low
Who [G]toil along the [D]climbing [G]way
With [C]painful steps and [D]slow
Look [G]now, for glad and [C]golden [G]hours
Come [Am]swiftly on the [D]wing
O [G]rest beside the [D]weary [G]road
And [C]hear the [D]angels [G]sing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
For [G]lo, the days are [D]hast'ning [G]on
By [C]prophet bards fore[G]told
When [G]with the ever-[D]circling [G]years
Comes [C]round the age of [D]gold
When [G]peace shall over [C]all the [G]earth
Its [Am]ancient splendors [D]fling
And the [G]whole world send [D]back the [G]song
Which [C]now the [D]angels [G]sing
{end_of_verse}
